    answer: 'Yes. Medicare Part B covers outpatient mental health services — including psychotherapy, psychiatrist visits, and partial hospitalization programs — at the same 20% coinsurance rate as physical health services. Federal mental health parity law requires Medicare to apply equal cost-sharing for mental and physical health care. Licensed psychologists, clinical social workers, and nurse practitioners can provide covered mental health services under Part B.',
  },
